tart":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"UDGEyJkyTy"}],"key":"x5YI2GbQ3H"}],"urlSource":"blog.md","dataUrl":"/blog.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"PbeECmTUzd"}],"key":"f6dqsXcV7U"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recent blog posts","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"qC4DEGDRUt"}],"identifier":"recent-blog-posts","label":"Recent blog posts","html_id":"recent-blog-posts","implicit":true,"key":"fXAo2yVQRw"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/lock-files","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The slow boring of hard boards in open source","key":"jpBU9KLTyC"}],"key":"WOFfIUkQ3v"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"yQcdDow1PR"}],"key":"gmVLVqHbT3"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"eLd3ZZP1TZ"}],"key":"WuZuS27axK"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"PyiakMpjsL"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"Rd0c1kOHnv"}],"key":"MoBVryIxqK"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"oyLo7Q5UQb"}],"key":"Cu2W7h5H4V"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","key":"Qh2pk607wE"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"KDPlk4bCL5"}],"key":"RPSFMrORlx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"m5BlpasCAK"}],"key":"D2VoSGNux3"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"o1kkuSUAr0"}],"key":"i35YTKQHDQ"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"t3PEGfGJVo"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"KaqT2kxNzY"}],"key":"e4cqGoN1be"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"zNRz03V90F"}],"key":"HoQsbJXBO3"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","key":"OVUYPFAYCt"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"tTy8bL5zXp"}],"key":"rP8JTXIiPl"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"pRxnHfaPiA"}],"key":"pQ5iVj3cf7"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"jhRU57vooo"}],"key":"uvQlNkbGP2"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"x8LecjLmY5"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"rSrQHB1mpQ"}],"key":"SY75TXF00I"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"SNZF0iGEhA"}],"key":"cUZMYevkmO"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","key":"g3nu13Kcrn"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"NVZKaMOUDr"}],"key":"owm8a6k0Nw"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"vSSExaj1UY"}],"key":"LGQIloevAh"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"x9xOsQhfpr"}],"key":"UmeSsUtcZW"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"gHZ0ppKG9D"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"uJ8zITIrSG"}],"key":"A0BVMrPEgT"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"BqmDzktKZO"}],"key":"MEERSQnvPG"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","key":"fEMVV4GQe4"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"Mho5CiqKCq"}],"key":"Josc1lZNrR"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"KvSmo0YKO9"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"moixNy7q5x"}],"key":"UFe7UuaZPF"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"PltQzjy03G"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"WWBytjn1cn"}],"key":"e5kNp3i8nq"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"wJ3pqg4EBl"}],"key":"b85GhSyJIu"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"BVxRkFKdTp"}],"key":"rxhL84uvxO"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"oBAUREZLeu"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"CBi1F4o1db"}],"key":"lbFa9mcY8N"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"oE93bNKvzN"}],"key":"Z7w2JfIkBY"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","key":"KyKnrFw4mf"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"MliUiRTr5J"}],"key":"Lls8BjG3xL"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"WfsyVN8GVQ"}],"key":"Z7lq4CTEgl"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"tj0tJ4Q5FX"}],"key":"XnrkkR9B75"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"EHNXTQkr6y"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"chs14Io266"}],"key":"AMpMqlEvyP"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"Rt1sZ9NPbB"}],"key":"hgRO1Hgaz6"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","key":"fRsxrcfAiz"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"baKSnsM1Xq"}],"key":"s2qAhearfy"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"uN8iQjMxDh"}],"key":"dJODRb7tks"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"TSE43zX3wQ"}],"key":"VSQD8NKRTN"},{"type":"text","value":"January 14, 2025 | ","key":"OXXHYfhwpc"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"RZThI6cINg"}],"key":"N8vJcr7ZoH"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"PjxgfyUwkU"}],"key":"TDl0NXm8m9"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jec","key":"gbogzgpXxR"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/bluesky","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How I'm trying to use BlueSky without getting burned again","key":"XdKRJkXiB2"}],"key":"xzGNQhEKwS"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some quick thoughts on moving from Twitter/X to BlueSky and how I'll try to use social media after being burned once by Twitter.\n","key":"rTKOotLeAf"}],"key":"wV5ttpVcme"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"pKYdmpLy1c"}],"key":"DPHwco5Emg"},{"type":"text","value":"November 22, 2024 | ","key":"mKROXXvatI"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"UaripkiDNM"}],"key":"nt73aqphhO"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"Ash7OIxCfp"}],"key":"hHFs2brBUU"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/bluesky","key":"VHFkWQiwgS"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/blog-list","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better blog lists with the MyST AST","key":"S6og68Hi1E"}],"key":"CtJJXzpcsA"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nOn my journey to learn more about writing with [the new MyST engine](https:///mystmd.org), I built upon [my recent update to my blog infrastructure](./programmatic-myst-with-jupyter.md) and made some improvements to my blog post list.\nHere's what it looks like now:\n\n````{note} Click here to see how it looks now\n:class: dropdown\n```{postlist}\n:number: 3\n```\n````\n\nHere's a quick rundown","key":"SyObWoxvsf"}],"key":"sLeYZ7NAAX"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"MD60vRDKpR"}],"key":"gm9MZFg1vF"},{"type":"text","value":"November 09, 2024 | ","key":"sPxUVZWf5s"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"jDdWHgrh85"}],"key":"xrGUo0ytbn"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"EBp1s4pwYc"}],"key":"BP1UZqMLmQ"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/blog-list","key":"G4B26P2MON"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate MyST with Jupyter and insert it into content programmatically","key":"p6ABkQV469"}],"key":"F9R7c9m9zX"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\n\nWhile I've been [converting my blog to use the new MyST engine](./mystmd-with-the-blog.md), I discovered a useful MyST feature. It's not yet possible to [natively parse Jupyter Markdown outputs as MyST](https://github.com/jupyter-book/mystmd/issues/1026) but there's a workaround if you don't mind generating a temporary file.\n\nThe trick is to _write to a temporary file_","key":"A0kfnkYQYK"}],"key":"TZ8F5NxDin"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"VRi1dNkEnr"}],"key":"tGXDuBaJNy"},{"type":"text","value":"November 04, 2024 | ","key":"cmrdJUxAmw"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"cApMNfIbot"}],"key":"d1lQZrU4ZO"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"J9YUn7LIpG"}],"key":"mSFwyOlAnK"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","key":"TFDrJj8O9j"}],"key":"ojOfFmZ3gD"}],"key":"sDKtYFbFO2"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"next":{"title":"About me","url":"/about","group":"Welcome"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}